.TH OROC-INIT 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.1.4" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-init \- Create a new project. If the path is not provided, the new project will be created in the current directory.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc init [<project\-dir>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Create a new project. If the path is not provided, the new project will be created in the current directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C, \-\-config\fR
only create the config file
.TP
\fB\-n, \-\-name\fR
project name
.SH NOTES
.PP
By default this command creates a starter `oro.toml`, `src/index.html`, `src/index.js`, `src/serviceworker.js`, and `.gitignore`. Use `\-\-config` when you only want the config scaffold without the example app files.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBoroc init my\-app\fR
create a new starter project in ./my\-app
.TP
\fBoroc init \-\-config\fR
write only the default oro.toml into the current directory
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1)
